  "question": {
    "text": "The perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining $P(1,4)$ and $Q(k, 3)$ has $y$-intercept - 4. Then a possible value of $k$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tWzXr",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "T7Q21",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TsAwP",
      "text": "\n$-2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zZdfL",
      "text": "\n$-4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Slope of bisector $=k-1$\nMiddle point $=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{k}+1}{2}, \\frac{7}{2}\\right)$\nEquation of bisector is\n$y-\\frac{7}{2}=(k-1)\\left(x-\\frac{(k+1)}{2}\\right)$\nPut $\\mathrm{x}=0$ and $\\mathrm{y}=-4$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow k=\\pm 4\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
